<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'VPC Peering & Private Connectivity'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>VPC Peering & Private Connectivity</h1>
  <p>Connected two VPCs via VPC Peering, configured route tables, enabled private database access, and monitored traffic with VPC Flow Logs in CloudWatch.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>VPC Peering</span><span>Route Tables</span><span>VPC Flow Logs</span><span>CloudWatch</span><span>Private Connectivity</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/vpc-peering.png" alt="VPC Peering Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>secure private connectivity between two VPCs</strong> using VPC Peering — enabling cross-VPC communication without internet exposure.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created a <strong>VPC Peering connection</strong> between Lab VPC (10.0.0.0/16) and Shared VPC (10.5.0.0/16).</li>
      <li>Updated <strong>route tables</strong> in both VPCs for bidirectional traffic.</li>
      <li>Configured the <strong>inventory application</strong> to connect to the private database.</li>
      <li>Enabled and analyzed <strong>VPC Flow Logs</strong> in CloudWatch.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔵 Lab VPC (10.0.0.0/16)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Hosts inventory <strong>EC2 application</strong></li>
          <li>Route: 10.5.0.0/16 → Lab-Peer</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🟣 Shared VPC (10.5.0.0/16)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Hosts <strong>private database</strong> (no IGW)</li>
          <li>Route: 10.0.0.0/16 → Lab-Peer</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔗 Peering Connection</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>VPC Peering (Lab-Peer)</strong> — Private link</li>
          <li>SG allows MySQL port 3306</li>
          <li><strong>Flow Logs</strong> — CloudWatch monitoring</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created <strong>VPC Peering connection</strong> between Lab VPC and Shared VPC.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Accepted the peering request and updated <strong>both route tables</strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Configured <strong>Security Groups</strong> to allow MySQL (port 3306) across VPCs.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Tested <strong>inventory app to private database</strong> connectivity successfully.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Enabled <strong>VPC Flow Logs</strong> and analyzed traffic patterns in CloudWatch.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Created <strong>VPC Peering connections</strong> for inter-VPC communication.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>route tables in both VPCs</strong> for bidirectional routing.</li>
      <li>Enabled <strong>private connectivity</strong> without internet gateways or NAT.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>VPC Flow Logs</strong> for network traffic visibility and troubleshooting.</li>
      <li>Avoid <strong>overlapping CIDR blocks</strong> between peered VPCs.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

